1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,001
This damBreak was run by hand: blockMesh, checkMesh, setFields and interFoam, typed one at a time. Its logs remember every step, but there is no Allrun to do it again.

2
00:00:10,001 --> 00:00:13,874
Allrun Steps shows a case's Allrun as steps. This case has none, so it offers to write one from the logs.

3
00:00:13,874 --> 00:00:20,407
Every log begins with the command that wrote it and when it started, so the steps come out in the order they ran, with their options. The Allrun is previewed below as you go.

4
00:00:20,407 --> 00:00:26,404
checkMesh only reports, so it is left unticked. Tick it to keep the check.

5
00:00:26,404 --> 00:00:31,894
FoDE adds one step: restore 0 from 0.orig after meshing, so every run starts from the same fields.

6
00:00:31,894 --> 00:00:39,796
An Allclean comes with it, to put the case back the way it was before a run.

7
00:00:39,796 --> 00:00:48,157
Create writes both scripts, executable, and opens the Allrun in the editor.

8
00:00:48,157 --> 00:00:55,397
Allrun Steps now reads it: every step done, from the logs that were already there.

9
00:00:55,397 --> 00:00:59,257
Now the case runs from its Allrun. The logs are still there, so FoDE offers to clean first.

10
00:00:59,257 --> 00:01:03,257
The steps window follows the run: a step reads Running while its log is being written, then Done.
